      "body": "## Summary (author-provided intent, AI-edited)\n\n> Improve MXFP8 compile-test execution on SM103 by selecting the supported\n> weight-gradient accumulation mode. This test-only change also applies to\n> other SM10x devices and does not add hardware support.\n\n## Why\n\n> **AI-assisted technical notes:** `test_mxfp8_linear_runs_outside_plain_eager`\n> compiles an `MXFP8Linear` with its default `inplace_wgrad_accum=True`.\n> Traced backward explicitly rejects that configuration, so the two compiled\n> cases fail before checking the weight gradient. The compile cases need the\n> supported non-in-place path; the checkpoint cases can retain their current path.\n\n## What changed\n\n> **AI-assisted technical notes:** Set `linear.inplace_wgrad_accum = False` only\n> when this test chooses `torch.compile`. This changes the test setup and does\n> not change the production configuration or the checkpoint cases.\n\n## Testing\n\n> **AI-assisted test notes:** On B300 (SM 10.3), with PyTorch\n> `2.16.0.dev20261102+cu130` and Triton 3.9.0, the two compile cases on base\n> `485c065cb248863bf2e2c65588becd6d7a8bcf83` fail at the in-place WGRAD guard.\n> With this change, the four compile/checkpoint combinations pass, and the\n> complete test file reports 25 passed. The tested file was a byte-identical\n> copy of the changed file.\n>\n> ```text\n> python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q candidate_test_mxfp8_linear.py::test_mxfp8_linear_runs_outside_plain_eager\n> # 4 passed\n> python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q candidate_test_mxfp8_linear.py\n> # 25 passed\n> ```\n>\n> The local `pre-commit run --all-files` run passed the formatting, lint and\n> other available hooks; the link checker skipped because `lychee` was absent.\n> Pyrefly could not pass locally because that environment lacked the project\n> dependencies. The same Pyrefly 0.45.1 check with project dependencies on an\n> isolated source copy completed with 0 errors and 2 warnings.\n",
